# oracle: pair_style pace/extrapolation with a full (non-linear) active set: a self-made two-element B-basis (Cu, Ni; FinnisSinclair, density inner cutoff, the unlike pair's ChebPow radial basis given in one of its two blocks; scripts/oracle/pace-extrapolation-fixtures.py) on a random fcc Cu-Ni cell, the grade every 3 steps of NVE and every minimizer step (min_pre_force)
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE)
# Measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error engine vs native thermo 1.0e-13, atoms 1.8e-15.
# oracle-inputs: pace_al_cuni.yaml pace_al_cuni.asi
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 3.55
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             type 1 type/fraction 2 0.4 8812
mass            1 63.546
mass            2 58.693
displace_atoms  all random 0.08 0.08 0.08 7731 units box
pair_style      pace/extrapolation chunksize 64
pair_coeff      * * pace_al_cuni.yaml pace_al_cuni.asi Cu Ni
fix             grade all pair 3 pace/extrapolation gamma 1
compute         gmax all reduce max f_grade
compute         gave all reduce ave f_grade
velocity        all create 500 991 loop geom
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press pxx pyz c_gmax c_gave
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          3
run             12
unfix           1
unfix           grade
fix             grade all pair 1 pace/extrapolation gamma 1
min_style       cg
minimize        0 0 6 20
